    "body": "Measurements so far (issue-worker-medium, Windows MSVC, rustc 1.99, shared/loaded machine, so +-20% noise). Cmd (a) = `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test repair_model --no-run`, empty target.\n\n| Variant | cold build | target/ |\n|---|---|---|\n| baseline (opt 2 deps, full debug) | 395 s | 2833 MB |\n| debug = line-tables-only, deps debug=false | 409 s (overlapped an install) | 1616 MB (-43%) |\n| + sccache, empty cache | 203-294 s | 1616 MB |\n| + sccache, warm, other worktree path | 177 s (opt 2) | 1616 MB |\n| deps opt-level 1 (parallel build, noisy) | 216 s | 1536 MB |\n| deps opt-level 0 (parallel build, noisy) | 114 s | 1619 MB |\n\n- (b) `camcraft-motion --lib --no-run`: 73 s / 435 MB baseline; with sccache 40 s empty cache, 47 s warm (mostly our own crates).\n- sccache across two worktree paths: 161 of 207 cacheable Rust compiles hit (77.8%). It hits ONLY when CARGO_TARGET_DIR is not set as an env var (sccache hashes CARGO_* env vars; with the env var, 0 hits). The 46 misses are our 7 path crates plus build scripts/proc-macros (62 non-cacheable). C code (flecs via cc): `CC=\"sccache cl\"` failed because cl is not on PATH outside vcvars; not cached.\n- Dep opt-level vs run time, motion finish3d: opt2 46.7 s, opt1 48.7 s, opt0 142 s. flow: 47 s / 50 s. adaptive_band, app import, pocket3d_hsm are too short to tell (<2 s).\n- Linker: rust-lld works (rc 0) but relink 2.1 s vs link.exe 2.4 s; switching linkers rebuilds build scripts (~110 s). Not worth it - left out.\n- Panic backtraces keep file:line with line-tables-only (checked).\n\nMissing: warm-cache cold build with the final settings (opt 1 + cache), `cargo xtask gate quick` timing, batch gate timing, C-code caching. Done-means (3x faster, target <= half) is not confirmed: target is 57% of baseline, cold build ~2.2x with a warm cache at opt 2.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
