    "body": "SKULL: slice \"route C/C++ through sccache in the gate\" is not needed - no PR. Finding:\n\n- cc-rs 1.8.0 (the version in Cargo.lock) already does this itself: `Build::rustc_wrapper_fallback()` (src/lib.rs ~4092) reads `RUSTC_WRAPPER` and, when its file stem is `sccache`/`cachepot`/`buildcache`/`kache`, prefixes it to the C/C++ compiler (both the default-compiler path and an explicit `CC` path). `cargo xtask gate` already exports `RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache` (PR #913) and cargo's build scripts inherit it, so `flecs_ecs_sys`'s `cc::Build` (build.rs:236, one file: `src/flecs_rust.c`, which includes flecs.c) goes through sccache with no xtask change. The user's preset wrapper and `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1` apply to it for free, and `cargo xtask release` already clears RUSTC_WRAPPER, so packaging does not use it.\n- The \"1 C/C++ request\" #914 could not identify is exactly that flecs compile (a miss cold, a hit warm), so the claim in #914 point 5 (\"flecs C is not cached on Linux\") was wrong.\n- Measured now (Linux, 8 cores, load ~1 idle-ish, fresh worktree, own default target/, `sccache --zero-stats` first, `cargo xtask gate test repair_fills_the_hole_and_undo_restores_the_facet_count --crate camcraft-app --binary repair_model --exact`): 122 s gate step (134 s wall), 195 requests, C/C++ 1 hit / 0 misses (100%), Rust 191 misses (cache for Rust was cold for this toolchain/profile). The flecs C compile was a cache hit in a different worktree path.\n- Windows/MSVC: cc-rs applies the same fallback on the default-compiler path, so it should hold there; #913's `CC=\"sccache cl\"` failure was the explicit-CC route, not this one. Not measured on this box.\n\nLeft open: a unit test pinning that the gate env keeps `RUSTC_WRAPPER` as the only routing knob is not worth adding; the open #900 targets (target size, 3x warm build) are unchanged. Claim released.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
