    "body": "Checked for a pick (effort:medium worker, 2026-11-13). Nothing concrete is owed on this issue that is not already shipped or tracked elsewhere: sccache opt-in, line-tables-only debug, deps debug=false and deps opt-level 1 are on main (Cargo.toml); the linker switch was measured and rejected (2.1 s vs 2.4 s relink, forces a build-script rebuild); C code is cached via cc-rs's RUSTC_WRAPPER fallback (see mkinney's comment). What remains are unmet measurement targets (target/ 54-57% of baseline vs half; warm build ~2.2x vs 3x), and the structural lever (folding test binaries, cutting app coupling) is #919 and its sub-issues, outside this issue by its own text. No code change identified, so no claim taken and no PR. Suggest the maintainer either closes #900 as partly done with the numbers above or re-measures after #919's sub-issues land.",
